.TH HTab 1 "2009-03-03" "HTab 1.4" "USER COMMANDS"
.SH NAME
HTab \- terminating tableaux system for hybrid logic
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B htab
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
HTab is a theorem prover and model builder for
the hybrid logic equipped with the down-arrow binder,
and the universal and difference modalities. HTab is
guaranteed to terminate for all formulas of the
language without down-arrow binder.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\-h, \-?, \--help
display help
.TP
\-f FILE, \--input-file=FILE
obtain input formulas from FILE instead of STDIN
.TP
\-q, \--quiet, \--silent
suppress all normal output
.TP
\-s, \--log-state
display the internals of the tableaux and the rules used during the calculus
.TP
\-b [0|1], \--semantic-branching=[0|1]
disable/enable semantic branching (default is enabled)
.TP
\-u [0|1], \--unit-propagation=[0|1]
disable/enable unit propagation (default is enabled)
.TP
\--inclusion-blocking-chain
enable chain-based inclusion blocking (default mode)
.TP
\--inclusion-blocking-global
enable global inclusion blocking (has precedence over chain-based blocking)
.TP
\--immediate-blocking
enable blocking from the start (default is disabled)
.TP
\-t T, \--timeout=T
run for at most T seconds. Default is no limit.
.TP
\-m FILE, \--save-model=FILE
generate a model for the input formula, into the file model.out
.TP
\-S PATTERN, \--statistics=PATTERN
print statistics during of after the execution.
A valide pattern is of the form:

METRICS:INTERVAL:METRICS

The `:INTERVAL:METRICS` argument is optional
and declares metrics that will be printed at
regular intervals (e.g. `:100:r' shows the
number of rules applied so far, every 100
iterations of the algorithm).
.br
METRICS is made of one or more of the following
values:

c : number of closed branches

r : number of rules applied

The default is ':0:c'

.SH FILES
.I ~/.htabrc
configuration file
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Run HTab without semantic branching nor unit propagation:
.B htab
\-b 0 \-u 0 \-f formula.frm
.PP
.TP
Run HTab in quiet mode:
.B htab
\-q \-f formula.frm
.PP
.SH INPUT FILE SYNTAX
The grammar for the files accepted by the prover is specified below. Comments
of the form '{' ALPHANUMERIC '}' are accepted anywhere in the file.

FILE := 'begin' FORMULAS 'end'
.br
FORMULAS := FORMULA | FORMULA ';' FORMULAS
.br
FORMULA :=
.br
  'true' | 'false' |
.br
  PROPOSITION | NOMINAL | VARIABLE |
.br
  NEGATION | CONJUNCTION | DISJUNCTION | IMPLICATION | DIMPLICATION |
.br
  BOX | DIAMOND | AT | UBOX | UDIA | UDIFFBOX | UDIFFDIA |
.br
  '(' FORMULA ')'
.br
PROPOSITION  := 'P' NUMBER | 'p' NUMBER
.br
NOMINAL      := 'N' NUMBER | 'n' NUMBER
.br
VARIABLE     := 'X' NUMBER | 'x' NUMBER
.br
RELATION     := 'R' NUMBER | 'r' NUMBER
.br
NEGATION     := '!' FORMULA | '-' FORMULA | '~' FORMULA
.br
CONJUNCTION  := FORMULA '&' FORMULA | FORMULA '^' FORMULA
.br
DISJUNCTION  := FORMULA '|' FORMULA | FORMULA 'v' FORMULA
.br
IMPLICATION  := FORMULA '->' FORMULA
.br 
DIMPLICATION := FORMULA '<->' FORMULA
.br
BOX          := '[]' FORMULA | 'box' FORMULA | '[' RELATION ']' FORMULA
.br
DIAMOND      := '<>' FORMULA | 'dia' FORMULA | '<' RELATION '>' FORMULA
.br
AT :=
.br
 NOMINAL ':' FORMULA | '@' NOMINAL FORMULA  |
.br
 VARIABLE ':' FORMULA | '@' VARIABLE FORMULA
.br
DOWN         := 'down' VARIABLE '.' FORMULA | down '(' VARIABLE FORMULA ')'
.br
UBOX         := 'A' FORMULA
.br
UDIA         := 'E' FORMULA
.br
UDIFFBOX     := 'B' FORMULA
.br
UDIFFDIA     := 'D' FORMULA


See also the example formulas in 
.I /usr/share/doc/htab/examples
or
.I /usr/local/share/doc/htab/examples
.

.SH .htabrc SYNTAX
The .htabrc file must contain arguments as given to the HTab executable.
